{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Difficult Relationships"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Writing a Letter"}, {"type": "position", "content": 8}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 8}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Exchange information about unlikely events or fairly certain conditions that will be fulfilled in present, past or future  in spoken or written texts and in work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Writes effective, clear, and detailed texts about different concrete and abstract topics, showing good organization and appropriate use of language to create the intended effect for the purpose and context."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn11le08ob08re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Writing Tip: Using Clauses With -<span class=\"italic\">ing</span>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use the <span class=\"italic\">\u2013ing</span> form like a noun, like an adjective or like a verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Smoking</span> is dangerous. </span>(noun) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I have a long  <span class=\"strong\">working</span> day. </span>(adjective) <br/> <span class=\"italic\">I'm <span class=\"strong\">working</span> late today</span>.</span> (verb)<br/><br/>  When you use  <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> as a   <span class=\"underline\">noun</span>, you may or may not put an   <span class=\"underline\">article</span> before it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "  For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Marketing</span> is a very inexact science.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">The marketing</span> of the product will continue for a few months yet.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can also use it as a  <span class=\"underline\">noun phrase</span>. <br/><br/> For example:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Speaking to an audience</span> is always terrifying.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Swimming after work </span>is very refreshing.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " You can use the <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span> form before a noun when it is an  <span class=\"underline\"> adjective</span>.<br/><br/>  For example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"> I was met by a <span class=\"strong\">welcoming party</span> at the airport. Let's go to the <span class=\"strong\">meeting room</span>.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "  You use the <span class=\"italic\">\u2013ing<an>/s form after <span class=\"underline\">prepositions</span>.<br/><br/>  For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Before coming</span>, you need to speak to Tanya.<br/> <span class=\"strong\">After discussing</span> it with her, I've changed my mind.<br/> I'm looking forward <span class=\"strong\">to seeing</span> her again.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Living your life without someone to share it with can be lonely. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Give Margaret a chance of unearthing a hidden gem for you. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Before you think of dismissing my idea, why don't you give me a call and we can chat about the process."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Get back in the game and start dating."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Writing an Informal Letter"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You write informal letters to friends and family.  They often include causal language and are written more like a conversation rather than an organized piece of writing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The most common salutation in an informal letter is <span class=\"italic\">Dear</span>, followed by a comma."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The first part of the letter should explain to the recipient why you are writing to them."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The second part of the letter consists of the message you want to get across."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The final part of the letter is where everything is wrapped up<br/>Informal letters can end with a casual closing."}, {"type": "text", "content": " For example: <span class=\"italic\">Love</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">Missing you lots</span>, "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Informal letters convey emotions and feelings unlike formal letters.  They can also include contractions and short sentences."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to treat"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to deal with or think about something especially in a particular way"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How's life been treating you lately?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob08aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use in a casual letter about relationships."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to show someone up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to embarrass someone by being superior"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Stop showing the rest of us up!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob08aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "inseparable"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " not able to be separated "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She and I have been inseparable ever since our first date."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn11le08ob08aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "portly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "having a round and somewhat fat body "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: She laughs at my corny jokes and even thinks that my \u201cportly\u201d frame is adorable. "}, {"type": "audio", "content"